From 5c46e3e94c320248dce171599b67941b664878d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basin Battle <basin@battle>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:19:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] A game object can be drawn longer along one axis, and doodads
 the data has no row for can be placed

A GameObject whose GAMEOBJECT_FLAGS carry 0x40000000 (0x80000000) is drawn longer along its
model's X (Y) axis by the factor its GAMEOBJECT_LEVEL holds as an f32's bits, on top of
OBJECT_FIELD_SCALE_X on every axis (entities::stretch): at its dressing, a building preview's
re-create and the scale ease. So one rope piece spans any length at the thickness its scale
gives it. A factor that isn't a finite number from 0 to 100 draws it unstretched.
GameObjectDisplayInfo gains rows from 60000 for doodads the client ships only as models
(benilla-formats EXTRA_DISPLAYS, mirrored by Elwynn Survival's server); a row the data has is
never replaced. The first is the dwarven dig site's rope, Tripwire's wire. HasActionCombat() is 13.
